@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@ AdrenoMetal publishes a Metal device through `MTLAddDevice`. It translates AIR t
 A render pass that fails encoding returns an encoder and reports a command-buffer error. This supports callers that cache encoder methods.
 
 
-Unused owned image backing is reused by pooled and dedicated images. Extra spares share a 256 MiB budget per device and expire after ten seconds. Plain backing of at least 256 KiB is retired on the existing room worker, with a 128 MiB queue limit. An allocation failure releases queued backing before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks keep their release ordering. First-use allocations can still prepare new pages.
+Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Image spares expire after ten seconds and are reclaimed on allocation failure or memory pressure; they have no byte limit. Unused buffer reservations share a separate 64 MiB device budget across memory types. The room worker rechecks demand and reuses a spare of the same pool and memory type before allocating. If foreground completions restore room during allocation, the new owned buffer stays spare with its address object intact. Owned blocks are released by the runtime's free thread; its 64-item queue falls back to the releasing caller when full. An allocation failure releases spares and waits for posted frees before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks keep their release ordering. First-use allocations can still prepare new pages.
+
+The runtime keeps command counts in each open encoder and reuses unchanged resource-residency facts. Merge scratch can be lent to later encoders of the same command buffer, with its original barriers and leases. A shadow may remain current across command buffers only for tracked private memory owned by the runtime; heaps and external memory retain their required copies. `sheng-metal-flow=1` separately enables lowering, direct commit submission and pipeline warming for experiments; it defaults to off, and pipeline waits remain exact.
 
 ## Cache and priority
 
@@ -43,6 +45,64 @@ See the [GPU adaptation procedure](/porting/gpu) for staging and board inputs.
 
 Frame diagnostics retain allocation, command, completion and GPU/display timing. Pixel capture is disabled. See [GPU frame diagnostics](/porting/gpu-diagnostics).
 
+The isolated iPhone27 integration keeps the upstream GMEM memory-side colour
+swap correction and lazy transient attachment policy, with the GMEM trace ABI
+and colour fixture from the same source series. Its full-test worker covers
+device and imported host images without changing another thread's render mode.
+Icon-service event65 notifications follow upstream6416a76. Source/host checks do
+not establish A840 system presentation; that acceptance remains a device result.
+
 `sheng-wallpaper-freeze=1` isolates wallpaper rendering. A Poster renderer retains its first successfully drawn and stored IOSurface output of at least two million pixels, then parks later command buffers before runtime submission. Parked buffers remain committed and unscheduled; their owners and queue leases stay retained. Previously submitted work completes normally. PosterBoard, backboardd and other clients continue submitting. The mode defaults to off.
 
 Detailed latency records identify slow encoder calls, callback invoke addresses and resource destruction. Kernel sampling of the render, encode and completion threads correlates upstream waits.
+
+
+For the local fixed Private Turnip heap route, patch0038 copies raw unsigned
+image words directly to Metal's tiled layout, retaining the original copy-in,
+keep/merge, external-memory and unsupported-view paths. The image owns its
+integer view and the tracker names sampled reads and storage writes. GPU026's
+117 local runtime tests pass, including raw floating/sRGB bits, padding, the real
+heap construction, release/reuse and independent writers. A840 performance is
+pending and must compare render-pass time and mutable-view mode as well as the
+removed intermediate image-to-buffer conversion. Pipeline waits remain Exact;
+the optional flow, lowering worker and warm pass remain off by default.
+
+The local Darwin transport retains one client and 1 ms maximum fence requests
+with the original absolute deadlines. Normal allocation/import skips age-based
+cache eviction; successful fence observers reserve one item and release it
+outside the retirement mutex. Cache reuse, growth and pressure flushing skip
+reserved items. Busy/error completion retains exact remaining lease ownership.
+Memory-pressure flushing and pending-fence retention are unchanged. Standalone
+CPU mappings use API7 with command0, within the existing33-record profile budget.
+
+
+The initial GMEM tile-store command-stream reservation now returns its Vulkan
+error before entering unchecked packet emission. EndRenderPass frees its
+temporary state and skips later GPU commands; EndCommandBuffer returns the
+existing recording error before appending cache-flush packets. This handles
+the observed null write after a failed BoMap, while preserving the underlying
+mapping failure and032 cache policy. It is not a general GPU reset or a claim
+that every command-stream allocation failure has been handled.
+
+
+Synchronous Metal resource, function and pipeline creation now uses the existing
+compact frame span records (kinds22–29, retained at250us), including nested
+descriptor/runtime/reflection work. Outer calls record CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID
+through the previously unused type18 c/d fields, with tid=1 only for a valid
+monotonic CPU delta; older and unmeasured rows retain zero. This distinguishes
+caller work before an encode batch is flushed from work waiting on the encode
+thread. It does not change batching, scheduling, GPU commands or shader caches.
+The optional pipeline journal no longer queries task/thread statistics when it
+is disabled. Hardware latency improvement remains to be measured.
+
+
+The iPhone24A446 frame observer reads IOMFBServer pending-update and Mach display
+timer state only after matching the loaded QuartzCore UUID and original vtables.
+SpringBoard main-thread observations use the existing bounded Mach/stack reader
+at20ms in a separate springboard-waits.trace for at most ten minutes. Each process
+records its boot UUID, Mach timebase and image bases; samples are not atomic snapshots.
+The render/encode observer has a6144-sample bound. Per-Vulkan-call Mach CPU
+profiling is opt-in with NATIVE_METAL_DRIVER_CPU_PROFILE=1; batch boundaries
+retain cumulative CPU nanoseconds, validity and query duration in type14.
+Type29 holds display-state fragments, type30 process/boot identity and type31
+the actual profiling policy. Hardware performance remains separately measured.
